  "design": "An 80x80 post on an 80x80 sill, a quick connector's Ø18 x 28 cross hole 25 from the end in each of two diagonal cores (-20, -20) and (20, 20): on face -y 20.00 across the other way, and on face +y 20.00 across, each 20 in from its face and 8 past its core. The same from two quick connectors in a recipe's set, at its two holes. One as sold on a 40x40 post: +y at the centre line. A 40x80 post's cores (0, -20) and (0, 20): faces -y and +y, no offset. A hole 15 deep: it stops 5 short of the core, an error, no hole. A position (50, 0) off the 80x80 end, a mount whose plane is not the joint's: an error each, no hole",
